response:
Extend the sides of the pentagon. By drawing the diagonals of the pentagon, five star-shaped pieces are formed. Each straight segment is therefore a side of a star, and is an example of an exterior angle. The sum of the exterior angles of any polygon is always $360^\circ$. In a regular pentagon, all exterior angles are equal. Therefore, the measure of each exterior angle of the pentagon is $360^\circ / 5 = 72^\circ$. <answer>Answer:$\boxed{72}$ degrees

